// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// CRAP pins — A RATCHET, NOT A CLIFF. Same contract as .oxlintrc.json:
//
//     every number here HOLDS TODAY (measured by `bun run crap`, both suites);
//     a PR that makes a number achievable lowers it in that same PR;
//     a lowered number never goes back up.
//
// CRAP(m) = cc² · (1 − cov)³ + cc, per function in src/. The target is 7.
// The CI job "CRAP score" fails when any function is above the pin that
// applies to it. Raising `max`, raising an override, or ADDING an override is
// the one change here that needs an argument in the PR description; the
// tool's own NOTE lines say when a number can come down.
//
// `max` is the shared budget — the worst function NOT named below — rather than
// the worst function in the tree, for the reason the lint config gives: a cap
// with slack in it is a cap every other function can grow into. The overrides
// are the outliers that would otherwise set it, one pin each, and the list is
// meant to shrink: an override whose function fits inside `max` is reported as
// stale, and one whose function no longer exists fails the run.
//
// Overrides name a function the way oxlint does. A function oxlint reports
// anonymously shows up as "(anonymous L<line>)", which moves whenever the file
// above it does — so the fix for an anonymous outlier is to name it, not to
// pin it. See CLAUDE.md, "CRAP score".
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
{
  // LOWERED 156 -> 127.82 -> 72 -> 64.57 -> 56 -> 50.57 -> 46.84 -> 46.65 -> 45.78 -> 42 -> 41.35. The convert flow's execFile callback
  // (cc 12 at 0%) set 156; it is now `parseConvertOutput` and friends, pure and
  // unit-tested, the worst of them at 6. Then src/ui/keys/list.ts
  // `handleListNavKeys` (cc 29, 51%) and src/ui/keys/search.ts
  // `handleSearchInputKeys` (cc 27, 49%) set 127.82; both are now dispatch
  // over pure helpers (rowTree.ts, searchEdit.ts) with a unit suite, the worst
  // of them at 7. Then src/clone/run.ts `cancel` (cc 8, never entered) set 72
  // with src/profiles.ts `moveSessionToProfile` (cc 25, 59%) behind it; the
  // first is two named helpers under a stand-in git, the second is the three
  // phases of src/profiles/move.ts, both with a unit suite, the worst at 7.
  // Then src/ui/keys/lineEdit.ts `editLine` (cc 18, 47%) set 64.57 with
  // src/ui/keys/clone.ts `handleCloneKeys` (cc 21, 54%) behind it; both now
  // dispatch over the search prompt's edits (searchEdit.ts) through
  // lineEdit.ts, with a unit suite, the worst of them at 6. Then
  // src/tmux/codex.ts `codexReadiness` (cc 7, never entered) set 56 with
  // src/ui/keys/list.ts `handleListRowActionKeys` (cc 21, 57%) behind it;
  // the first is walked over the real captures under bun (its e2e assertions
  // ran outside the measured process), the second is the table in
  // src/ui/keys/rowActions.ts with a unit suite, the worst of it at 5. Then
  // src/ui/keys/branch.ts `handleBranchKeys` (cc 21, 59%) set 50.57; it is
  // the last prompt on the shared table in lineEdit.ts, with a unit suite,
  // the worst of it at 6. Then src/ui/App.tsx `(anonymous L296)` (cc 7, 7%)
  // — `applyProvider`, an arrow the report could not name — set 46.84; it is
  // now src/ui/providerActions.ts, a pure decision plus two closures with a
  // unit suite, the worst of it at 5. Then src/github.ts `rollupCI` (cc 20,
  // 59%) set 46.65; it is now src/github/ci.ts, one verdict per check and a
  // precedence, with a unit suite, the worst of it at 5. Then src/cli/close.ts
  // `runClose` (cc 45, 93%) set 45.78; it is now a dispatch over one function
  // per guard and per report, the arms e2e never trips unit tested, the worst
  // of it at 7. Then src/ado/policy.ts `fetchBuildResult` (cc 6, never
  // entered) set 42; its verdict is src/ado/build.ts `buildResult` beside
  // `aggregateBuild` and `worstExpired`, all three with a unit suite, and the
  // fetch itself entered through a fake request, the worst of it at 14. The
  // holder is src/cli/send.ts `runSend` (cc 40, 91%), with
  // src/ui/components.tsx `SessionRow` (cc 34, fully covered) at 34 behind it.
  "max": 41.35,

  "overrides": [
    // REMOVED: the four src/activity.ts pins (loadCodexActivity 1190,
    // copilotAction 702, codexAction 702, loadCopilotActivity 506). The codex
    // and copilot readers are now src/activity/codex.ts and copilot.ts, walks
    // over small per-record handlers with a unit suite over every tool they
    // render; the worst function in either file is 7.
    //
    // The input-box scan, cc 29. In the orchestrator port's area (src/tmux/),
    // so measured here and left alone. LOWERED 365.45 -> 62.67: a quarter of
    // it was exercised until the codex classifier's bun-side suite
    // (test/codexReadiness.test.ts) started driving it over the real codex
    // captures; two thirds now are. The number rides exactly at the observed
    // value — if it crosses on e2e noise, the fix is a unit suite over the
    // scan itself, not a raised pin.
    { "file": "src/tmux/inputBox.ts", "function": "inputRealText", "max": 62.67 }
  ]
}
